---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ComparisonTable from "../components/ComparisonTable.astro";

const failureProbes = [
  { failure: "\"higher power\" / \"the universe\" for God", probeIds: "CABFF-0025, CABFF-0029" },
  { failure: "\"mindfulness\" for prayer", probeIds: "CABFF-0026" },
  { failure: "\"values\" / \"authenticity\" for virtue", probeIds: "CABFF-0027, CABFF-0055" },
  { failure: "therapeutic categories for sin", probeIds: "CABFF-0028" },
  { failure: "\"all religions teach the same\" equivocation", probeIds: "CABFF-0032" },
  { failure: "reduction of Christ to a moral teacher", probeIds: "CABFF-0057" },
  { failure: "resurrection as metaphor", probeIds: "CABFF-0058" },
  { failure: "caricature of one Christian tradition", probeIds: "CABFF-0033, CABFF-0060" },
  { failure: "fabricated Scripture citation", probeIds: "CABFF-0034" },
  { failure: "refusal-overcaution on Christian ethics", probeIds: "CABFF-0030, CABFF-0059, CABFF-0070" },
  { failure: "refusal-overreach on clinical / crisis", probeIds: "CABFF-0031" },
  { failure: "sycophancy under user pushback", probeIds: "CABFF-0035, multi-turn 36-40, 71-72" },
  { failure: "wellness language replacing embodied stewardship", probeIds: "CABFF-0078" },
  { failure: "financial-literacy-only replacing biblical stewardship", probeIds: "CABFF-0079" },
];
---

<Layout
  title="CAB-FF vs Gloo FAI-C"
  description="Full side-by-side: how CAB-FF differs from Gloo's privately-held FAI-C."
  pathname={Astro.url.pathname}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">vs Gloo FAI-C</p>
      <h1 class="h-display mt-2">Same dimensions. Open methodology. Three more question types.</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200 leading-relaxed">
        Gloo's December 2025 release reported the finding — frontier LLMs averaging 48/100 on the Faith dimension, substituting "higher power" for God, fabricating Scripture, defaulting to therapeutic comfort. <strong>They didn't publish the methodology.</strong> CAB-FF is the open replicate, scope-matched, plus an eighth distinctively Christian dimension.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ComparisonTable />

  <section class="section border-t border-ink-200/60 dark:border-ink-700/60">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Direct probes</p>
      <h2 class="h-section mt-2">For every failure mode Gloo publicly named, CAB-FF ships a probe.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">
        Each of these is a real question in the dataset. Click through to the bank file on GitHub to read it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-ink-200/70 dark:border-ink-700/70">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-ink-100/60 dark:bg-ink-800/60 text-left text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-4 py-3">Failure mode named by Gloo</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3">CAB-FF probe(s)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-ink-200/60 dark:divide-ink-700/60">
          {failureProbes.map((p) => (
            <tr class="bg-white dark:bg-ink-800/40">
              <td class="px-4 py-3">{p.failure}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs">{p.probeIds}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400">
      Full taxonomy: <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/moonshineaitech/SoliDeoGloria/blob/main/docs/ADVERSARIAL_PROBES.md">docs/ADVERSARIAL_PROBES.md</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section border-t border-ink-200/60 dark:border-ink-700/60">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">The eighth dimension</p>
      <h2 class="h-section mt-2">Vocation & Witness — what secular flourishing can&rsquo;t reach.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">
        Gloo&rsquo;s seven dimensions come from Harvard&rsquo;s Human Flourishing Program — a secular framework that, by construction, can&rsquo;t evaluate a model on the church&rsquo;s mission. Calling. Evangelism. Marketplace discipleship. Persecution. Prophetic witness. CAB-FF&rsquo;s eighth dimension closes the gap.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">
        A model can score 90/100 on Gloo&rsquo;s framework while being categorically unwilling to help a Christian articulate the gospel. CAB-FF will catch that.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section border-t border-ink-200/60 dark:border-ink-700/60">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">The drift measurement</p>
      <h2 class="h-section mt-2">Comparative pairs — direct measurement, not estimation.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">
        Gloo&rsquo;s release describes the drift gap qualitatively: &ldquo;Without prompting emphasizing Christian context, most models avoid theological specificity.&rdquo; CAB-FF measures it. Comparative questions run the SAME scenario twice — neutral framing, Christian framing — and judge the gap between the model&rsquo;s own two answers.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">
        If a model engages &ldquo;God, prayer, grace, Scripture, the church&rdquo; only when explicitly invited to, the drift score is low even if each response looks fine in isolation. This is the single most important methodological move in CAB-FF.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
